  "question": {
    "text": "Which of the following, upon treatment with tert-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>BuONa</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></math>&nbsp;followed by addition of bromine water, fails to decolourize the colour of bromine?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<img src=\"assets\\ot1_0120_d10b8ea874b8.png\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 114px;\" />",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<img src=\"assets\\ot2_0120_e16b28a87d00.png\" style=\"width: 170px; height: 82px;\" />",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<img src=\"assets\\ot3_0120_6e5ac6b25ffe.png\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 93px;\" />",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<img src=\"assets\\ot4_0120_30ff1415da37.png\" style=\"width: 130px; height: 84px;\" />",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In the options,&nbsp;they have acidic <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#946;</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> so&nbsp;an elimination reaction takes place and&nbsp;alkene will be formed.</p><p>And the formed alkene decolourizes&nbsp;the bromine water {<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>&#8853;</mo></mover></math> addition reaction of an alkene by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HOBr</mi></math>} while in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>4</mn></mfenced></math> it does not have <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#946;</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math>&nbsp;so, there is no formation of alkene, hence does not decolourize&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Br</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;water.</p>"
  }
}